  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing the aspiration level (mean of outcomes ignoring probabilities), calculating differences, and then comparing the probability of positive differences. The individual does not mention the aspiration level, nor do they compute or refer to differences between outcomes and a mean. Instead, their reasoning is based on the absence of loss in A (only gains or zero), and the risk of getting nothing in B. They focus on the structure of outcomes (only gains in A vs. risk in B) and the higher amount in A. There is no reference to the mean of outcomes, nor to positive differences from a mean. The justification does not follow the rule of the decision reason — it is based on risk of loss and certainty of gain, not on the probability of positive differences relative to an aspiration level. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as defined. The reasoning is conceptually different and does not align with the stated rule of the reason.",
